# ============================================================
# Environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev; set the same in your host's
# dashboard (e.g. Vercel -> Project Settings -> Environment
# Variables) for deploys. Never commit real values.
# The app reads exactly these four variables - nothing else.
# ============================================================

# --- TMDB (metadata; free account) ---
# themoviedb.org -> Settings -> API -> "API Read Access Token" - the long
# JWT, not the short "API Key". Sent as a Bearer header, server-side only.
TMDB_API_READ_TOKEN=

# --- Torrentio + Real-Debrid (stream resolution) ---
# The app resolves streams through Torrentio's Real-Debrid-configured
# endpoint. TORRENTIO_CONFIG is the config path segment of a Torrentio
# install link, and it EMBEDS YOUR REAL-DEBRID API KEY - treat the whole
# value as a secret on par with the key itself. Server-side only; the
# app scrubs it from every error and log line, and the resolve URLs that
# contain it never reach the browser.
#
# To build it:
#   1. Get your Real-Debrid API key: real-debrid.com/apitoken
#   2. Open torrentio.strem.fun/configure - pick your quality filters
#      (recommended: filter out "cam" and "unknown"), choose RealDebrid,
#      and paste your key.
#   3. Copy the generated install link. It looks like:
#      https://torrentio.strem.fun/qualityfilter=cam,unknown|realdebrid=YOURKEY/manifest.json
#   4. TORRENTIO_CONFIG is everything between the host and /manifest.json
#      (no slashes at either end), e.g.:
#      qualityfilter=cam,unknown|realdebrid=YOURKEY
TORRENTIO_CONFIG=

# --- Supabase (auth + database; free tier) ---
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API. These two are safe in the
# browser by design (RLS is the security boundary) - they are the ONLY
# values that may ever be NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
